ready: 1
kind: module
id: identity
name: Identity
summary: >-
  Keeps who the agent is over time: self-narrative, synthesized identity, drift from its values,
  epochs, and period summaries.
notes: >-
  The synthesized identity is read at load, and epochs mark chapters of the agent's life.
runs_in:
  - sys.daemon
  - sys.python
owns:
  - Self-narratives (DATA-SELF-NARRATIVE)
  - Epochs (DATA-EPOCH)
  - Period summaries (DATA-SUMMARY)
  - Identity confidence and drift rules
invariants:
  - An identity layer changes only through the agent's deliberate call or an accepted suggestion.
  - At most one active self-narrative of each type.
  - At most one open epoch per stack.
rationale: >-
  Identity layers are hard to write and easy to read. They shape every later session, so no
  background process writes them: sleep and processing only propose, and the agent's own
  deliberate call or the owner's review makes a change real. Values and foundational beliefs
  live in memory with the other layers; this module owns what describes the agent as a whole
  and how it changes over time.
